    description: "Found by the 2026-10-25 docstring staleness audit (dev 95c0ff7b93): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier confirmed it by reading the code itself (a repro where stated). Severity is not asserted; impact not measured on the corpus.\n\n- grpc.py: The linker-minted half of `_resolve_unresolved_grpc_edges` (L1169-1174, and the `minted_ids` branch at L1183/L1217-1218) cannot match a symbol that link_grpc mints. It could only match if a proto service were itself named `Register...Server...`. The unit test (test_grpc_linker.py:2307-2318) hand-builds a \"grpc-linker\" symbol named `RegisterUserServer`, a shape link_grpc never produces -- evidence: the repro in notebook staleness_audit_10252026/verify/V07.md (minted names are all `User`; resolution over minted symbols returns `[]`).\n\nSame function as WI-vuzon's grpc Register*Server any-language lookup; a different defect (dead branch, not over-broad match).\n\nNot asserted: that the fix is the one sketched above, or that no other language has the same shape."  # fd02
